    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d894">

                <pb facs="1184" n="1174" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/11–845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-08">November 8,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received November 8—8:33 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1945. For Secretary of the Treasury from Adler.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>When asked at a press conference in Chungking on November 7 when the
                        Government could announce a fixed rate of exchange, Dr. P. H. Chang,<anchor
                            n="67" xml:id="d894-f1"/> the Government spokesman, said, “Of course,
                        the Government will readjust the present rate. But this question of rate of
                        exchange is a highly complicated matter. The Government will make a decision
                        after a careful and thorough study of the whole question is
                        completed.”</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>When asked why separate currencies have been issued in Manchuria and
                        Formosa, he said, “Before Japan surrendered, Formosa was a part of the
                        Japanese territory. During the war on account of Japanese maneuvers,
                        Manchuria was more or less isolated from China economically. Their
                        currencies were directly linked with the Japanese yen and should not be
                        considered as on the same basis as the puppet notes FRB (Federal Reserve
                        Board) or CRB (Chinese Reserve Bank). Therefore, it is necessary to issue
                        the so-called scripts <pb facs="1185" n="1175" xml:id="pg1175"/> as a
                        temporary measure to cope with the special situation in the northeastern
                        provinces and Formosa. China’s currency will be unified.” [Adler.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
